Problem Statement:
Phishing attacks exploit human trust by disguising malicious emails as legitimate communication. Traditional rule‑based detection systems struggle to adapt to evolving phishing tactics. This project aims to develop a machine‑learning model capable of automatically classifying emails as phishing or legitimate using textual and structural features.

Goals:

- Build a labeled phishing email dataset

- Extract meaningful textual features

- Train and evaluate multiple ML classifiers

- Achieve high precision and recall on phishing detection
